WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.250
(slow classical music)

00:00:04.986 --> 00:00:06.910
- [Woman] Greta is a 16-year-old girl

00:00:06.910 --> 00:00:09.944
who has inspired thousands
maybe even millions of people

00:00:09.944 --> 00:00:13.346
to stand up for both
themselves and the climate.

00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:15.390
- [Girl] She thought
everything was going in

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:16.790
the wrong direction.

00:00:16.790 --> 00:00:19.380
And now she's become a
really big role model

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:20.419
for a lot of people.

00:00:20.419 --> 00:00:22.980
- [Girl] I look up to her a
lot 'cause I think it's so cool

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:23.900
what she's doing.

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:26.640
- [Girl] It's time that
we actually stood up

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:28.680
for the climate and did something instead

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:30.436
of just sitting around.

00:00:30.436 --> 00:00:33.402
(slow classical music)

00:00:33.402 --> 00:00:35.010
- The climate crisis is

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:38.390
the biggest crisis
humanity has ever faced.

00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:42.462
And yet it has been ignored for decades.

00:00:42.462 --> 00:00:44.590
The older people usually

00:00:44.590 --> 00:00:46.700
say that we owe it to the young people

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:48.350
to give them hope.

00:00:48.350 --> 00:00:50.300
But we don't want you to be hopeful,

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:52.057
we want you to panic.

00:00:52.057 --> 00:00:55.660
They say that they love their children

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:56.550
above all else,

00:00:56.550 --> 00:00:58.840
and yet they are stealing their future

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:00.393
in front of their very eyes.

00:01:02.795 --> 00:01:05.234
The leaders who know that change is coming

00:01:05.234 --> 00:01:07.287
whether they like it or not.

00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:20.470
- [Announcer] One in four
Americans is skeptical

00:01:20.470 --> 00:01:21.790
of all the effects of climate change

00:01:21.790 --> 00:01:23.540
and thinks this issue's been exaggerated.

00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:25.560
- Environmental annihilation is coming

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:27.203
because we've been evil.

00:01:27.203 --> 00:01:28.480
- Do you know what this is?

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:29.778
It's a snowball.

00:01:29.778 --> 00:01:33.718
- Some people don't believe
in the climate crises,

00:01:33.718 --> 00:01:36.458
they don't understand that it's real.

00:01:36.458 --> 00:01:38.650
And I have to say

00:01:38.650 --> 00:01:40.230
that I understand them

00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:42.100
in a way because in the beginning

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:44.490
when I first found out about

00:01:44.490 --> 00:01:46.527
this I doubted that it was true.

00:01:46.527 --> 00:01:48.145
Because if it was true,

00:01:48.145 --> 00:01:51.250
then we wouldn't be talking
about anything else.

00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:53.460
That would be our first priority.

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:54.717
But it's not.

00:01:54.717 --> 00:01:57.732
People say it's like an abstract threat

00:01:57.732 --> 00:02:00.655
in the future, but it's happening now;

00:02:00.655 --> 00:02:02.650
we can already see the changes.

00:02:02.650 --> 00:02:05.438
We already have increased the temperature

00:02:05.438 --> 00:02:08.548
above pre-industrial levels 1.2 degrees.

00:02:08.548 --> 00:02:11.748
And everything's happening very fast now.

00:02:11.748 --> 00:02:13.270
We need to do something

00:02:13.270 --> 00:02:15.240
and act as if we were in a crisis

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:17.660
because otherwise people won't understand

00:02:17.660 --> 00:02:18.963
that we are in a crisis.

00:02:20.351 --> 00:02:24.188
- So Greta thanks to be with us, hi.

00:02:24.188 --> 00:02:26.592
You said many times I was like

00:02:26.592 --> 00:02:28.830
an invisible girl before.

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:30.170
But now you are very famous,

00:02:30.170 --> 00:02:31.290
everybody is here with you,

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:34.790
and they want you for the Nobel prize.

00:02:34.790 --> 00:02:38.053
How did you reach this point?

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:40.360
- In August,

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:44.450
last year I decided that this was enough.

00:02:44.450 --> 00:02:47.370
I sat myself down on the ground outside

00:02:47.370 --> 00:02:49.000
the Swedish parliament.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:51.420
And I school-striked for the climate.

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:55.271
I have said that I will
continue to school strike

00:02:55.271 --> 00:02:57.346
every Friday until Sweden is

00:02:57.346 --> 00:02:59.543
in line with the Paris agreements.

00:02:59.543 --> 00:03:01.417
That may take a long time.

00:03:01.417 --> 00:03:05.680
I will have to be patient
and to remind myself

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:07.173
of why I'm doing this.

00:03:08.329 --> 00:03:11.010
The symbolism of the school strike is

00:03:11.010 --> 00:03:14.260
that since you adults don't give a damn

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:16.315
about my future I won't either.

00:03:16.315 --> 00:03:18.850
Why should we care for our future

00:03:18.850 --> 00:03:20.481
when we might not have one?

00:03:20.481 --> 00:03:22.100
And why should we bother

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:26.364
to learn facts when facts
don't matter in this society.

00:03:26.364 --> 00:03:30.160
It's absurd that young people will have

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:32.270
to skip school.

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:35.840
And risk their own education
because they are scared

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:37.626
of not having a future.

00:03:37.626 --> 00:03:40.388
And I think that is a very strong message.

00:03:40.388 --> 00:03:42.820
- You have heard about

00:03:42.820 --> 00:03:43.808
a Greta Thunburg.

00:03:43.808 --> 00:03:44.959
- Greta Thunburg.

00:03:44.959 --> 00:03:45.839
- Greta Thunburg.

00:03:45.839 --> 00:03:46.772
- Greta Thunburg.

00:03:46.772 --> 00:03:47.660
- Greta Thunburg,

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:49.200
thank you very much for
joining us this morning.

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:50.729
- At first I was all alone

00:03:50.729 --> 00:03:53.602
and then people started joining me.

00:03:53.602 --> 00:03:57.600
And then it started
spreading to different places

00:03:57.600 --> 00:03:58.920
and then different countries

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:00.545
and then different continents.

00:04:00.545 --> 00:04:03.245
And then it became global.

00:04:03.245 --> 00:04:06.220
In December the UN had

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:08.385
a climate change conference,

00:04:08.385 --> 00:04:10.922
and there I held some speeches.

00:04:10.922 --> 00:04:13.027
We have run out of excuses

00:04:13.027 --> 00:04:14.830
and we are running out of time.

00:04:14.830 --> 00:04:17.840
I think that was also
when more people started

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:20.456
to found out about the school strikes.

00:04:20.456 --> 00:04:23.804
And then at the end of
January I was invited

00:04:23.804 --> 00:04:26.043
to the World Economic Forum.

00:04:26.043 --> 00:04:28.452
Our house is on fire.

00:04:28.452 --> 00:04:30.828
And also there I held a speech,

00:04:30.828 --> 00:04:33.064
which also went I think viral

00:04:33.064 --> 00:04:35.550
and those two I think,

00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:39.023
both those two were tipping
points of this movement.

00:04:40.087 --> 00:04:43.510
It has just escalated.

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:46.214
And it's going so fast
like I can't even keep

00:04:46.214 --> 00:04:47.930
up with it anymore.

00:04:47.930 --> 00:04:49.879
Now there is hundreds of thousands

00:04:49.879 --> 00:04:53.958
of children who are striking
from school for their future.

00:04:53.958 --> 00:04:55.252
(children chanting)

00:04:55.252 --> 00:05:00.198
(speaking foreign language)

00:05:00.198 --> 00:05:03.900
When I was 11,

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:06.971
I became very depressed.

00:05:06.971 --> 00:05:09.920
I stopped eating and I stopped talking

00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:11.700
and I stopped going to school.

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:13.400
It had a lot to do with

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:15.922
the climate and the environment.

00:05:15.922 --> 00:05:17.768
I started making changes

00:05:17.768 --> 00:05:19.543
in my own life.

00:05:20.610 --> 00:05:21.588
Like stop flying,

00:05:21.588 --> 00:05:24.740
stop eating meat and dairy.

00:05:24.740 --> 00:05:26.597
And stop buying new things.

00:05:26.597 --> 00:05:29.100
In order to be able to look myself

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:29.933
in the eye.

00:05:29.933 --> 00:05:33.662
I need to do something myself.

00:05:33.662 --> 00:05:36.284
I started talking with my parents.

00:05:36.284 --> 00:05:38.723
After awhile they decided
to do that as well.

00:05:45.794 --> 00:05:48.626
Before I started the school strike I was

00:05:48.626 --> 00:05:52.510
that person who was invisible.

00:05:52.510 --> 00:05:55.604
I never spoke unless I had to.

00:05:55.604 --> 00:06:00.099
And also I have Asperger's syndrome.

00:06:00.099 --> 00:06:01.360
I'm a bit different

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:02.890
from everyone else.

00:06:02.890 --> 00:06:05.601
When you have Asperger's
you also tend to have

00:06:05.601 --> 00:06:08.204
the capacity of being very focused

00:06:08.204 --> 00:06:10.834
and interested in some subjects.

00:06:10.834 --> 00:06:14.474
And that allowed me to focus

00:06:14.474 --> 00:06:17.113
on one thing for a very long time.

00:06:17.113 --> 00:06:19.532
I think that if I wouldn't have

00:06:19.532 --> 00:06:22.440
had Asperger's I don't
think I would have started

00:06:22.440 --> 00:06:23.450
the school strike.

00:06:23.450 --> 00:06:27.020
And I don't think I would
have been interested

00:06:27.020 --> 00:06:28.650
in the climates at all.

00:06:28.650 --> 00:06:30.680
Because if I would have
been like everyone else

00:06:30.680 --> 00:06:34.220
I'd just continued like
before not thinking twice

00:06:34.220 --> 00:06:36.605
about this, but now I can't do that.

00:06:36.605 --> 00:06:39.483
My conscious doesn't allow me to do that.

00:06:48.021 --> 00:06:50.504
(suspenseful music)

00:06:50.504 --> 00:06:55.466
(children chanting)

00:06:55.466 --> 00:06:59.700
I think this movement
could become very big;

00:06:59.700 --> 00:07:03.360
and I think that we have
just seen the beginning

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:05.710
because more and more people are going

00:07:05.710 --> 00:07:07.990
to start realize the
emergency of the situation,

00:07:07.990 --> 00:07:09.861
and they will get angry.

00:07:09.861 --> 00:07:13.057
And they will want to
do something about it,

00:07:13.057 --> 00:07:17.180
especially young people who
will understand eventually

00:07:17.180 --> 00:07:19.353
that their future is
being taken from them.

00:07:20.523 --> 00:07:23.720
Many people say that we are too young

00:07:23.720 --> 00:07:24.553
to do this,

00:07:24.553 --> 00:07:25.830
we shouldn't do this.

00:07:25.830 --> 00:07:26.663
And I agree,

00:07:26.663 --> 00:07:28.027
we shouldn't have to do this.

00:07:28.027 --> 00:07:30.728
But in the situation we are in now.

00:07:30.728 --> 00:07:32.680
We feel like we have to do this

00:07:32.680 --> 00:07:37.598
because we won't accept
you risking our future.

00:07:37.598 --> 00:07:40.230
If the adults won't take responsibility,

00:07:40.230 --> 00:07:41.568
then we will have to.

00:07:41.568 --> 00:07:44.818
(slow classical music)

